<task id="105" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Override (server)</title>
    <phase>4 Review and approval (WP4) — wave W4-2</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>in-progress</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Introduces a new privilege that lets one person accept a submission the rules blocked; authorization is security-class and the accept path must stay all-or-nothing.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Privilege check reuses an existing caller-scoped probe; the accept path is 049's; the remaining work is a guarded service and routes. The mechanism choice is escalated, not designed here.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P4-B</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>044, 049, 074</deps>
    <tags>bff, api, auth, security</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Let a user holding the "eBilling Override" privilege accept an internal submission despite a blocking failure, with a mandatory reason, as one person: the submission is persisted as accepted through 049's all-or-nothing path, the overridden finding stays visible to the reviewer marked Overridden, and one Decision Record is written via 074. Also provide the blocked-submission read (findings, canOverride) and the non-override alternative "Return to firm" for a blocked internal submission (owner question F-7).</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in ASP.NET Core authorization, Dataverse privileges and fail-closed design.</role>

  <goal>SubmissionOverrideEndpoints.cs and SubmissionOverrideService with GET blocked-submission state, POST override and POST return; one reusable override-privilege check (also used by 052 and 111 through canOverride); seeding proof that a caller without the privilege gets 403.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-37 (acceptance: Decision Record written; the overridden finding remains visible to the reviewer), FR-19 (user without the privilege sees no Override option and the server refuses an override call, 403; override writes a Decision Record), D-24 / D-39 (internal submissions only; one person), spec Assumptions ("a new security role privilege eBilling Override"), FR-26 / I-5, FR-30. 020: sprk_invoicesubmission (sprk_channel, sprk_processingstatus Received / Processing / Accepted / Rejected / Failed, sprk_outcomereasoncode, sprk_findingsjson, sprk_invoice). 049 persists accepted submissions (invoice, lines, portion, Signals) all-or-nothing and stores rejections as findings on the submission. Privilege building blocks: CallerRecordAccessProbe.CallerHoldsPrivilegeAsync (Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerRecordAccessProbe.cs:437 — caller-scoped OBO, uncached, fail closed), wrapped for routes by FinanceAuthorizationCheck.CallerPrivilege (Api/Filters/FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs:154); app-role precedent: the "SystemAdmin" policy (Infrastructure/DI/AuthorizationModule.cs:465). Dataverse has no custom privilege type, so a "security role privilege" needs a carrier (see escalation). 076 chose an admin mechanism for rule sets — read its notes and stay consistent. Policy keys: Spaarke.Core/Auth/OperationAccessPolicy.cs (100 added "ebilling.invoice.decide").</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Finance/SubmissionOverrideEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/SubmissionOverrideService.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/EbillingOverridePrivilege.cs (the one privilege check; name directional)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Auth/OperationAccessPolicy.cs (submission read / write keys, if the existing keys do not fit)</file>
      <file role="modify">049's accept path (file named in 049's notes) only if it cannot be called with an override marker — shared append point, see notes</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/FinanceModule.cs (shared append point)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/EndpointMappingExtensions.cs:376-377 (shared append point)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Finance/SubmissionOverrideServiceTests.cs</file>
