    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="044" status="pending">Submission records and channel</dependency>
      <dependency task="049" status="pending">All-or-nothing accept path and stored rejection findings</dependency>
      <dependency task="074" status="pending">Override action and recorder</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="074 ontology-r1 review K1/K3 (2026-10-17)">Recording billing Decision Records through BillingDecisionRecorder (074) brings two caller obligations.
- (1) Exactly-once. The writer is exactly-once only for retries made one after another; two concurrent calls with one decision id can both write, and a duplicate in an append-only ledger is permanent. So:
  - this task names its serialisation mechanism as an acceptance criterion. Examples: the job claims IIdempotencyService keyed by the decision id; an endpoint does a RowVersion-conditional status update and records only after it succeeds;
  - it adds a test for the concurrent same-id case.
- (2) Decider identity:
  - derive the deciding user from the authenticated principal, never from request input;
  - check invoice access through the UAC filter before recording;
  - pass no contact id. The recorder looks the contact up itself, as DecisionCommitService does; 074's fix round removes that parameter.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner D-101 (2026-10-17)">An overridden submission already has its invoice (In Review, held). Override releases it to approval, and its Decision Record files under that invoice (D-100 WriteBillingDecisionAsync).</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-76">eBilling Override is a Dataverse table privilege on a small dedicated table (owner decision D-76), checked once through CallerRecordAccessProbe.CallerHoldsPrivilegeAsync and failing closed; no security-role-name check and no app role. The table is created by an idempotent additive script under scripts/ebilling/ and captured into the solution source by the next deploy task; answer the root CLAUDE.md section 11 three questions for it in notes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-19, FR-37, root CLAUDE.md section 6">Override requires the privilege, checked server-side on every call, fail closed (no token, probe failure, unknown user = 403 ebilling.override.not_permitted). Reason required (400). One person: no second approval step.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-24">Only an internal-channel submission whose processing status is Rejected because of a blocking finding can be overridden; SPA submissions, Failed submissions and already-accepted ones are refused (409 with stable codes). A repeat override is a no-op with no new Decision Record.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-37, I-5">The override never deletes or rewrites the blocking finding: it is persisted as a Signal on the new invoice / line marked Overridden (with who, when, reason) and the line is Flagged for review.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-20, ADR-002">Acceptance runs through 049's all-or-nothing persist step; no second invoice-creation path. A failure leaves no partial invoice and the submission stays Rejected.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-30">Exactly one Decision Record per override via 074; the Return of a blocked submission records the outcome on the submission and a Decision Record only if 074's actions cover a submission subject.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-001, ADR-008, ADR-019">Own endpoints file; per-route filter plus RequireEbillingEnabled(); ProblemDetails with stable codes.</constraint>
    <constraint source=".claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md">Placement BFF (B1 caller identity, B4 live request); publish-size delta; no new HIGH CVE; no package.</constraint>
    <constraint source="074 fix-round adversarial pass (2026-10-18), caller obligations of BillingDecisionRecorder">Callers that record billing decisions through BillingDecisionRecorder must:
- Derive the resolved Signal ids and the policy version id server-side, from the decision's own invoice and lines. Never take them from the request. The writer accepts any existing Signal or policy version (074 review K-2).
- Record before mutating, or run the recorder's reads first. Its refusals that depend on Dataverse reads (unknown policy version, missing Signal, undetermined subject, contact read fault) happen after Preflight, so a caller that changes invoice status first can be left with a changed status and no Decision Record (K-3).
- Serialise decisions per invoice (one at a time per invoice). The recorder's "already recorded" check and its create are not atomic (K-4).
- Build Values the same way on every attempt (same types, same decimal scale), so that an honest retry hashes to the same content (K-5, unless 074's follow-up normalises decimals).</constraint>
  </constraints>

