  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Resolve the privilege-mechanism escalation with the owner BEFORE coding; read 076's notes, 049's accept path and stored rejection shape, 074's override action.</step>
    <step order="1">Implement the one privilege check (EbillingOverridePrivilege) and expose canOverride.</step>
    <step order="2">Routes under /api/finance/submissions/{submissionId} (names directional): GET blocked (channel, status, blocking findings with rule, version, clause, values read; canOverride; canReturn); POST override (decision id, reason); POST return (reason).</step>
    <step order="3">Override: validate state, call 049's accept path with the override marker, mark the blocking finding Overridden, record via 074, set the submission outcome. Return: per the F-7 answer.</step>
    <step order="4">Tests: privileged override happy path (invoice created, finding visible and marked, one record); no privilege 403; probe failure 403; reason missing 400; SPA / Failed / already accepted 409; repeat is a no-op; accept-path failure leaves no invoice; Return per F-7; contract tests 401 / 403 / disabled.</step>
    <step order="5">Seeding proof (missing-privilege guard): make the check return true unconditionally, show the 403 test fails, restore; record in notes.</step>
    <step order="6">dotnet build and dotnet test green; publish-size delta and vulnerable-package check recorded.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: this task's status cell to "✅ [done]".</step>
    <step order="8">Record deviations (mechanism, F-7 answer, routes) in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>🔔 Privilege mechanism (auth, security-sensitive — STOP and ask before coding). Options: (A) a Dataverse security role "eBilling Override" granting a privilege on a dedicated marker table, checked with CallerHoldsPrivilegeAsync (existing caller-scoped probe; administered with other Dataverse roles; needs one small schema addition, synced by 112); (B) an Entra app role on the BFF registration, checked like the SystemAdmin policy (no schema; administered in Entra, not Dataverse); (C) role-membership query by role name (no existing helper; name-based, fragile). Recommendation: A, matching the spec's "security role privilege" assumption and the existing probe; keep consistent with 076's choice where possible.</trigger>
    <trigger>Owner decided D-73 (F-7): any internal user with access to the submission's core record may Return a blocked internal submission, no privilege; only Override needs the eBilling Override privilege.</trigger>
    <trigger>If 049's accept path cannot take an override marker without restructuring, STOP and coordinate rather than duplicating invoice creation.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Spec section 11 row "Review / approval / export / rule endpoints"; privilege probe CallerRecordAccessProbe.CallerHoldsPrivilegeAsync and FinanceAuthorizationCheck.CallerPrivilege exist; no override route or privilege exists (grep "Override" under Services/Finance finds none).</existing>
    <extension>Reuses the existing probe or policy pattern and 049's accept path; a single privilege class is added so 052, 111 and the routes share one check instead of three copies.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>An internal user cannot accept a legitimately blocked invoice (e.g. a negotiated rate not yet in the rate card), so FR-19 and FR-37 fail and the only path is asking the firm to resubmit.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build, test</tool>
  </tools>

